  "details": "When a player enters a station, it is assumed they are locked to the GameObject. Occasionally, there are times when remote players do not see them in the station at all.\nThis is a very weird bug that was never noticeable before thanks to the combination of most stations are not mobile and network ik will force the player's position.\nHere is a world where you can sometimes see the issue.\nwrld_bff9dcbd-d43a-4815-8dea-ef0d9455feba \nThis world will force everyone into a station. This station then fakes the player position onto some location along the walls. Occasionally, you will see someone not along the wall, but clipping the floor. This usually affects late joiners, but can affect people currently in the world. The only known fix is for the remote person to exit the station and re enter.\nNote, this world has all stations as spawn objects. This might be related.",
